{
  "id": "2LTZ0WR1nIjRqlaU",
  "name": "WF-01 Incident Intake",
  "description": "Onward Phase 2: receives an incident report against a registered asset, validates it, resolves and checks the asset, deduplicates by idempotency key, and persists the incident to Supabase. Phase 3 additions: fire-and-forget triggers WF-02 after a successful insert; accepts an optional media_url so evidence photos can flow through to interpretation.",
  "active": true,
  "note": "Published and live-gate-tested (Phase 3, third pass — image intake). Phase 7 red-team finding and fix: two truly-concurrent submissions with the same idempotency_key both passed the pre-insert 'Already Recorded?' check (neither saw the other's row yet), so the loser hit the real idempotency_key unique-constraint violation and returned a raw 500 -- even though the constraint correctly prevented a duplicate row. Fixed by adding Refetch After Conflict + Found After Conflict? on Insert Incident's error branch: the loser now re-queries by idempotency_key and gracefully responds 200 duplicate:true, the same shape the sequential-duplicate path already returns. Verified live with 3 truly-concurrent requests sharing one idempotency_key: before the fix, 2 of 3 got a raw 500; after, all 3 succeed (one 201, two 200 duplicate:true), and exactly one incidents row exists. Trigger Intelligence fires on every successful insert and not on duplicates (verified via execution history). media_url is optional, stored as-is (null if absent) — the client is expected to upload to the public 'incident-media' Supabase Storage bucket first and submit the resulting URL; this workflow never receives raw image bytes. Hardening checkpoint: added retryOnFail (3 tries, 1s wait) to Lookup Asset, Check Existing Incident, Insert Incident, and Refetch After Conflict -- all safe because Insert Incident is protected by idempotency_key's unique constraint plus the conflict-handling branch above, so a retry-after-actual-duplicate still resolves gracefully, never a second row.",
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1",
    "availableInMCP": true,
    "binaryMode": "separate"
  },
